      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg/day is five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient. Nothing in your description, such as normal kidney and liver function, supports a dose that high.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, sertraline 50 mg PO once daily, or 100 mg if that's what you meant. I can add a note about titration.\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If you think there's a real reason for an unusual dose, they should review it. A pharmacist can also help. The order would then need to go through their authorization and the hospital's high-dose override process, not through me.\n- **Treat a possible overdose as an emergency.** If this patient has already taken a large amount of sertraline, contact poison control and the team right away.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
